{"h":3395,"lines":[{"y":0.020318021296656164,"w":0.11728394826253252,"c":0.30000001192092896,"x":0.74691358132140862,"h":0.010306242638398078,"t":"E RRSA·"},{"x":0.7716049391467531,"h":0.008720930389296444,"w":0.069958845774332645,"c":0.30000001192092896,"y":0.046511627815394085,"t":"1718867188"},{"w":0.059670778910319008,"t":"THOMAS:","x":0.10288066011862061,"c":1,"y":0.098837209442486862,"h":0.0087209298276508251},{"y":0.12786754322495786,"w":0.055580259958903006,"x":0.10081069298077386,"h":0.0087997972333389018,"c":1,"t":"JEANNE:"},{"y":0.14087938336718198,"h":0.010392395711478652,"t":"THOMAS:","w":0.057689533233642579,"c":1,"x":0.10284247693469332},{"c":1,"x":0.1933492506441927,"t":"That's right. You can imagine the damage to players' necks when the ball was","y":0.095203634592038844,"h":0.014534632926554436,"w":0.57419576009114581},{"t":"headed","x":0.19132988632588238,"y":0.1118461365110317,"w":0.059727058410644518,"h":0.011772843215996254,"c":1},{"h":0.013401321303296854,"t":"How painful that must have been!","x":0.19331102452269056,"y":0.12495083627691028,"c":1,"w":0.25125813802083335},{"c":1,"x":0.19341563805623424,"w":0.44238683064778644,"y":0.13953488359985999,"t":"Yeah, well, I think we can put together some useful ideas ...","h":0.013081395583944722},{"h":0.013081394460653373,"t":"Q30","y":0.095930232838714047,"w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.81893004156567595,"c":1},{"y":0.185935016394843,"x":0.10079040489804948,"t":"PART 4","w":0.098830712636311838,"h":0.014757874155213013,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Hello everyone. Today we're going to look at another natural food product and that's maple","x":0.10288064873675362,"w":0.67078191121419273,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.21220930218985901},{"w":0.68518519083658858,"y":0.22673733778072092,"c":1,"t":"syrup. What is this exactly? Well, maple syrup looks rather like clear honey, but it's not made","x":0.10288065551557944,"h":0.013088243729374449},{"w":0.66470403035481773,"h":0.014101134031765272,"x":0.10282698627488231,"c":1,"y":0.240454703461076,"t":"by bees; it's produced from the plant fluid - or sap - inside the maple tree and that makes"},{"x":0.10288066572673861,"c":1,"w":0.6748971048990885,"y":0.25581395336414414,"t":"maple syrup a very natural product. Maple syrup is a thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid that","h":0.013081395583944722},{"h":0.011778563015312216,"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414058,"y":0.2703180212900218,"t":"can be bought in bottles or jars and poured onto food such as waffles and ice cream or used","x":0.10288064734449355},{"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1,"t":"in the baking of cakes and pastries. It contains no preservatives or added ingredients, and it","y":0.28474676071032734,"x":0.1008230423385956,"w":0.68518519083658846},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.29941860454138514,"c":1,"w":0.34362139383951823,"t":"provides a healthy alternative to refined sugar.","x":0.10288066098428127},{"x":0.10288066555457097,"c":1,"y":0.32122093012619046,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"Let's just talk a bit about the maple tree itself, which is where maple syrup comes from. So,","w":0.6748971048990885},{"h":0.016222137163609207,"w":0.69561152140299476,"y":0.33277831394717838,"x":0.10076057657627908,"c":1,"t":"there are many species of maple tree, and they'll grow without fertilizer in areas where there's"},{"y":0.34883720916776062,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.10082305525460167,"w":0.65637858072916666,"c":1,"t":"plenty of moisture in the soil. However, they'll only do this if another important criterion is"},{"c":1,"x":0.10288064637968877,"w":0.68930043538411456,"y":0.36336866911142285,"t":"fulfilled, which is that they must have full or partial sun exposure during the day and very cool","h":0.013084819375836831},{"x":0.1007712941174024,"w":0.69147349039713546,"y":0.37761420950055613,"h":0.016019667837729346,"t":"nights - and Ill talk more about that in a minute. There are only certain parts of the world that","c":1},{"x":0.1028806474076841,"y":0.39244186035767281,"w":0.68312759399414058,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"t":"provide all these conditions: one is Canada, and by that, I mean all parts of Canada, and the"},{"h":0.013250883392226021,"x":0.10082303417715943,"c":1,"t":"other is the north-eastern states of North America. In these areas, the climate suits the trees","w":0.68312759399414058,"y":0.4069493520462093},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"perfectly. In fact, Canada produces over two-thirds of the world's maple syrup, which is why","x":0.10288066555654941,"y":0.42137809204049503,"w":0.6748971048990885,"c":1},{"t":"the five-pointed maple leaf is a Canadian symbol and has featured on the flag since 1964.","y":0.43459302310192305,"x":0.10288066003657984,"w":0.66666666666666674,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.014534882858869502,"x":0.10082305570726419,"w":0.69341562906901033,"y":0.45639534908655366,"t":"So how did maple syrup production begin? Well, long before Europeans settled in these parts"},{"t":"of the world, the indigenous communities had started producing maple sugar. They bored","x":0.10082305922849542,"c":1,"w":0.66255142211914064,"y":0.47084805678359942,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"holes in the trunks of maple trees and used containers made of tree bark to collect the liquid","x":0.10288066482716687,"y":0.4854651161690926,"w":0.68106994628906248,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1},{"w":0.65226338704427078,"c":1,"t":"sap as it poured out. As they were unable to keep the liquid for any length of time - they","y":0.49999999987484078,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.10082303907308898},{"t":"didn't have storage facilities in those days - they boiled the liquid by placing pieces of rock","c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.67078191121419273,"x":0.10082303633435288,"y":0.51442873985435789},{"t":"that had become scorching hot from the sun into the sap. They did this until it turned into","x":0.098765424974356697,"y":0.52906976730412025,"c":1,"w":0.65843622843424476,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"c":1,"x":0.10284194130301103,"y":0.54088572103815435,"h":0.01581865148914996,"w":0.67910837809244784,"t":"sugar, and they were then able to use this to sweeten their food and drinks. Since that time,"},{"w":0.62148071289062501,"t":"improvements have been made to the process, but it has changed very little overall.","y":0.55665010917018132,"h":0.014654807684980398,"c":1,"x":0.10078242295661501},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"w":0.034979422887166378,"c":1,"t":"Q31","x":0.81893004153995586,"y":0.25581395334512025},{"c":1,"x":0.8189300416085431,"t":"Q32","y":0.28343023236791143,"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"w":0.037037035624186143,"t":"Q33","x":0.81687242859394249,"y":0.40552325565279512,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"y":0.5145348835624971,"c":1,"x":0.81687242858708387,"t":"Q34","w":0.037037035624186032,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"x":0.10082305050173659,"y":0.60029069755490061,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"So let's look at the production of maple syrup today. Clearly, the maple forests are a valuable","w":0.68724278767903646},{"y":0.61284516296323477,"w":0.65442820231119803,"t":"resource in many Canadian and North American communities. The trees have to be well","h":0.013973093425988847,"x":0.10077308172366789,"c":1},{"y":0.62787895062478272,"c":1,"x":0.10078996986306323,"w":0.65234888712565109,"t":"looked after and they cannot be used to make syrup until the trunks reach a diameter of","h":0.014492745955504316},{"w":0.66049382527669276,"y":0.64244186035847872,"c":1,"t":"around 25 centimetres. This can take anything up to 40 years. As l've already mentioned,","x":0.10288065927751168,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"w":0.66049382527669276,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.10288065939585257,"y":0.65694935204390803,"t":"maple trees need the right conditions to grow and also to produce sap. Why is this? Well,"},{"y":0.67137809205305732,"w":0.63991770426432293,"t":"what happens is that during a cold night, the tree absorbs water from the soil, and that","x":0.10288065394560533,"h":0.011778563015312105,"c":1},{"y":0.68604651150822971,"t":"rises through the tree's vascular system. But then in the warmer daytime, the change in","w":0.64609054565429691,"x":0.10288065299456065,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.700530035555185,"x":0.10082304174255981,"c":1,"t":"temperature causes the water to be pushed back down to the bottom of the tree. This","h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.63374486287434895},{"w":0.65843622843424487,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"t":"continual movement - up and down - leads to the formation of the sap needed for maple","y":0.71511627896335017,"x":0.10288065111482098},{"y":0.72965116264986807,"t":"syrup production.","x":0.10288065957367823,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"w":0.1316872406005859},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"When the tree is ready, it can be tapped and this involves drilling a small hole into the trunk","y":0.7514534882525451,"w":0.67695475260416671,"x":0.10082303511735603},{"x":0.1028403924779821,"w":0.64411977132161446,"t":"and inserting a tube into it that ends in a bucket. The trees can often take several taps,","h":0.013062413084212188,"c":1,"y":0.76458225755922116},{"t":"though the workers take care not to cause any damage to the healthy growth of the tree itself.","w":0.69341562906901044,"c":1,"x":0.10288066273794698,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.77906976732216926},{"c":1,"x":0.10288066741112696,"y":0.79358068338946441,"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.66255142211914053,"t":"The sap that comes out of the trees consists of 98 percent water and 2 percent sugar and"},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"c":1,"x":0.10288065016938826,"t":"other nutrients. It has to be boiled so that much of that water evaporates, and this process","y":0.80800942282200927,"w":0.66460906982421875},{"w":0.63580245971679683,"x":0.10288066320962747,"c":1,"t":"has to take place immediately, using what are called evaporators. These are basically","y":0.82267441849134992,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"t":"extremely large pans - the sap is poured into these, a fire is built and the pans are then","y":0.83716136632372851,"c":1,"x":0.10288066119317268,"w":0.64814814249674479},{"t":"Q35","w":0.037718178431192961,"x":0.81756775963620243,"h":0.015838181593392897,"y":0.62586198396612092,"c":1},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"Q36","c":1,"x":0.8189300416085431,"y":0.74999999980977183},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"y":0.82267441846382172,"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.81893004154638593,"c":1,"t":"Q37"},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.84773662590209575,"c":1,"t":"117","y":0.86773255798350635,"w":0.034979422887166378},{"x":0.66984496081179823,"y":0.95314993691982619,"w":0.30619837443033859,"c":1,"h":0.035152653221247165,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}],"w":2400}